[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Exception and Error Handling
REQ_PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-16-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Fatal Exception Error Handler
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide default handlers for exceptions.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want exceptions which I did not handle explicitly (by mistake or on purpose) to be caught by a default handler, defined either by Zephyr OS or by myself.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Default handler for fatal errors
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide default handlers for fatal errors that do not have a dedicated handler.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Assigning a specific handler
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to assign a specific handler for an exception.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Assigning a specific handler for a fatal error
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to assign a specific handler for a fatal error.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Triggering a fatal error in the current context
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism for software to raise a fatal error attributed
to the current execution context.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Triggering a fatal system error
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism for software to raise a fatal error that is
treated as unrecoverable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Fatal error reason
STATEMENT: >>>
When a fatal error handler is invoked, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a reason code identifying the type of error.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Default fatal error policy
STATEMENT: >>>
When a fatal error occurs and the application has not provided its own fatal error
handler, the Zephyr RTOS shall halt the system.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: System reset on fatal error
STATEMENT: >>>
Where reset on fatal error is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall reset the system upon a
fatal error instead of halting it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Recovery from a fatal error in thread context
STATEMENT: >>>
When the application-provided fatal error handler returns following a fatal error
attributed to a thread, other than an unrecoverable error, the Zephyr RTOS shall
terminate the offending thread and continue operation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: No recovery from an unrecoverable fatal error
STATEMENT: >>>
When the application-provided fatal error handler returns following an unrecoverable
fatal error, the Zephyr RTOS shall halt the system.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-16-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Fatal errors in interrupt context are unrecoverable
STATEMENT: >>>
If a fatal error occurs in interrupt context, other than a thread stack overflow
detected during interrupt exit, then the Zephyr RTOS shall treat the error as
unrecoverable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-5
